  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); fund-balance roll-forward 1,675,162 -> 2,063,507; no beginning cash printed (no prior-year balance sheet), ending cash = governmental funds cash 2,053,818 + county treasurer cash 9,689 (p4). Business-type lines from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7); Sewer capital outlay (6,200) printed as a negative nonoperating item is recorded as spending; net position 728,455 -> 777,202. Proprietary cash flows from the Total column (p9); the Electric column labels cost of power as 'Payments to employees' (p8), recorded as printed. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (totals equal the government-wide figures), business-type lines from p1. Detail: General Fund from the budgetary comparison schedule (p10). The General Fund departments combining schedule (p14) is only partly in the trim: its General and Fire columns are on p14, but the continuation page with the Rescue, Library, Parks and Total columns (report p44) is missing, so the department/object schedule is not recorded (it would double count the budget schedule). General Fund transfers from other funds and Street Fund capital outlay are budget-only (actual 0), not recorded. Utility funds have no supplementary schedule, so no utility detail. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
